Two Xeon packages of two cores with two threads each, numbered as Linux does
on such machines: each package's first threads (0-3), then their siblings
(4-7). Thread 7 is offline, so it is missing from /proc/cpuinfo, has no
topology, and its core lists only thread 3. Each package has its own
coretemp chip. The packages are listed by id with their own threads, and the
first thread of each core stands for its temperature.
